x86_64-linux  four differences, all recorded shapes. cxx1's element loops `__cxx1_vec_new_1S`/`_del_1S` against clang's inline code; the C1/D1 forms of the in-class members; and the guarded static itself, which clang keeps as `_ZZ1fiE3arr` with `_ZGVZ1fiE3arr` and a `__cxa_guard_abort` cleanup, where cxx1 names the object by its own unique static symbol and guard, as every static-local case here does. The functions the program declares agree.
